I use FreeMind (
http://freemind.sourceforge.net/wiki/index.php/Main_Page)  to keep
track of my dungeons.  FreeMind is a tree structured "mind mapping"
piece of software that allows free association.  I built a template
that I start fesh for each game.  All of the dungeon level numbers are
on the right of the tree, and my DragDrop objects are to the left.  The
objects I drag/drop are major level areas like shops, altars, temples,
castle, Fort Ludios entrance, all stuff like that.  Then I append notes
to each item with details like shop type or what Sokoban held.

If you want to try it you can d/l FreeMind for free and use the
template I created.  I put my template and screenshots here if you want
to check it out: www.deverter.net/nh

